WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.800 align:start position:0%
In February 2026, an American company
sought permission to mine minerals from

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:13.700 align:start position:0%
the bottom of the Pacific Ocean. The
proposed site lies thousands of

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:18.400 align:start position:0%
kilometers from the United States in
waters beyond any country's national

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:22.600 align:start position:0%
jurisdiction. Under the international
system governing the deep seabed,

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:26.500 align:start position:0%
activities there are supposed to be
managed collectively, but the company

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.200 align:start position:0%
did not seek permission from the
international body. It turned to

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.300 align:start position:0%
Washington instead.
The Trump administration had already

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:39.100 align:start position:0%
moved to accelerate American seabed
mining, hoping to secure valuable

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:44.700 align:start position:0%
minerals without depending on foreign
suppliers. For Washington, this made

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:49.200 align:start position:0%
strategic sense. China dominates the
processing of many critical minerals,

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:53.500 align:start position:0%
and the United States wants
alternatives. Yet, there is a larger

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:58.400 align:start position:0%
issue here.
For decades, America has been one of the

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:03.200 align:start position:0%
strongest defenders of an international
maritime system that limits what

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:08.500 align:start position:0%
individual countries can claim or
control. Its naval power has helped keep

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:13.200 align:start position:0%
shipping routes accessible while its
diplomats have repeatedly challenged the

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:17.900 align:start position:0%
excessive claims [music] of others.
But things have changed. Washington is

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:23.600 align:start position:0%
now breaking the rules it once helped
set up, and the timing is particularly

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:28.400 align:start position:0%
consequential because rivals elsewhere
are testing the rules in their own ways.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:34.100 align:start position:0%
The conditions under which ships can
travel, resources can be extracted, and

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:38.800 align:start position:0%
maritime claims can be enforced are
increasingly contested.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:43.800 align:start position:0%
Russian length vessels are suspected of
damaging undersea cables. The Houthis

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:49.500 align:start position:0%
are threatening shipping through the Bab
el-Mandeb. Iran is charging ships for

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:54.600 align:start position:0%
passage through Hormuz, while President
Donald Trump briefly floated the idea of

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:59.892 align:start position:0%
an American fee there as well. Even
Indonesia proposed a toll system in the

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:03.592 align:start position:0%
Strait of Malacca, though the proposal
was later withdrawn.

00:02:01.792 --> 00:02:07.892 align:start position:0%
No one has formally announced the new
partition of the seas, and that is

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:13.492 align:start position:0%
precisely what makes it easy [music] to
miss. The oceans are not being divided

00:02:10.692 --> 00:02:19.292 align:start position:0%
with lines on a map, at least not yet.
Instead, the old order is being

00:02:15.692 --> 00:02:22.992 align:start position:0%
dismantled one exception at a time.
When you spend a lot of time following

00:02:21.192 --> 00:02:27.492 align:start position:0%
world events, there's always another
crisis to understand, another conflict

00:02:25.592 --> 00:02:32.192 align:start position:0%
to follow. And between alarming
headlines, endless commentary, and the

00:02:29.892 --> 00:02:36.692 align:start position:0%
temptation to keep doom scrolling, it's
easy to feel overwhelmed by everything

00:02:34.892 --> 00:02:41.692 align:start position:0%
happening around us.
I caught myself in that spiral recently,

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:45.992 align:start position:0%
just scrolling through updates late at
night, one headline after another. At

00:02:44.092 --> 00:02:49.292 align:start position:0%
some point, you're no longer staying
informed. You're just feeding the

00:02:47.992 --> 00:02:53.292 align:start position:0%
anxiety.
Talking through moments like these with

00:02:50.992 --> 00:02:58.492 align:start position:0%
a therapist can really help set
healthier boundaries. Better Help,

